{
  "name": "first-run",
  "about": "The agent-first first run, one screen state per storyboard frame: Welcome; Pick your agent (only the agents found here, most preferred first: Hermes, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, then the rest; one Connect each, none connected by itself, each naming the file it changes; the connected agents' own sign-ins and keys in the same order; nothing found: install an agent or use the CLI); Add your other computers (optional sign-in: your other computers and your cloud, Not now); on a signed-in Mac that shares its screen, Share this Mac's screen (Screen Recording and Accessibility, Allow each, a check once granted, Not now); and Try it in the lead agent (a request to paste, waiting until the agent used Cua; no agent: a one-click first Space, Linux first, then Omarchy and macOS only where they run and fit). No plan is shown. Home's to-do list after Skip for now treats signing in as optional. Each case patches the base input; every app draws firstRun.view's words and must say the same. Install the Cua CLI shows between Pick your agent and Add your other computers only while the app's bundled CLI is not on this computer (a disk-image install): the exact file, the PATH line when one is needed, Install or Not now, and the result; Local builds name cua-local.",
